Complete test checklist
 Submit run via Swagger (note run id)
 Worker claims it (check logs)
 Kill the worker (docker kill)
 Wait 5 seconds
 Different worker claims it (logs show new epoch)
 Run completes (status changes to completed)
 Event log has no duplicates (one TOOL_RESULT per tool call)
 Database shows run finished with owner_worker_id = NULL
 Nondet values are journaled (NONDET_RECORDED event)
 Restart killed worker (docker compose up -d worker)
 Three workers in fleet again
If something goes wrong

Run stuck as running after worker killed:

powershell
docker compose logs worker

Check for exceptions. Most likely: database connection issue or epoch mismatch.

No second worker picks up the run after lease expires:

powershell
docker compose exec postgres psql -U anchor -d anchor -c "SELECT id, status, lease_expires_at, now() FROM runs;"

If lease_expires_at < now() but still status = running, the reclaim query might not be working. Check loop.py claim_one() has the updated SQL.

Duplicate executions in log:

powershell
curl http://localhost:8000/api/runs/<id>/events | jq '.[] | select(.type == "TOOL_RESULT") | .payload.tool_name' | sort | uniq -c

If any tool appears twice with the same args, reconstruction failed. Check reconstruct() is being called before execution.

